# Line-ending and diff handling.
#
# This file exists because `demo-data/` is now tracked and `core.autocrlf` is on for
# most contributors here. Without it git treats a PDF as text, "helpfully" rewrites LF
# to CRLF on checkout, and the file that lands is a corrupt PDF — which
# `tests/unit/test_demo_documents.py` would then fail on with a parse error rather than
# anything that names the cause. Committing binaries without this is worse than not
# committing them at all.

# Normalise text in the repository, and let each platform check it out natively.
* text=auto

# Documents and archives are bytes. Never touch them, never try to diff them.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary

# Sample messages carry RFC 5322 headers and are parsed byte for byte by the mail
# intake tests. Held at LF so a checkout on Windows does not change what is being
# parsed — the `Message-ID` dedupe and the MIME boundaries both depend on it.
*.eml   text eol=lf

# Kept at LF because the intake tests assert on exact cell content, and a CSV whose
# rows gained carriage returns compares unequal for a reason nobody would guess.
*.csv   text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they will not run: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter whose name ends in a carriage return.
*.sh    text eol=lf
